ontent\\\": \\\"Asks about someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Who</span> did this poster?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">What</span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks about something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">What</span> did programs focus on?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Where</span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks about a place\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Where</span> did you put your keys?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">When</span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks about the time something happened\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">When</span> did you leave?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Why</span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks about the reason \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Why</span>  did you write that?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">How</span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asks for the method in which something is done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">How</span> did you program that game?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What did I mean with this two subjects?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What did you get with this information?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for any programmer you know."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Get more information about what is like working as a programmer and about POP and OOP."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down all the new information you got."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Interchange this information with your classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for a real programmer"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I get information from his/her real experience."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write down a report"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about what I learnt with my class. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "procedural "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "related to any establish way for doing something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am going to talk about procedural programming."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "programmer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who works with computer programs"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, procedural programming refers to a programming technique that lets programmers decide the way to start a program."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "course "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the direction that something moves along"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Programming languages are made to permit users to define the course of the program."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "property "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a special characteristic of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For example, a type of car that has properties as wheels, glasses and doors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "appliance "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a household or device created for a particular use"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That computer is the object of a class of appliance."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sequentially "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that occurs in a particular order"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, procedural programming refers to a programming technique that lets programmers decide the way to start a program and put its items into practice sequentiallyProgramming "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le02ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Hi, my name is Danna and I am going to talk about procedural programming known as POP, and object oriented program also known as OOP. What did I want to tell you about these two subjects? Well, procedural programming refers to a programming technique that lets programmers decide the way to start a program and put its items into practice sequentially; that means that it focuses on the flow of activities step by step. Thus, the main emphasis stays on decomposing issues into small parts and solve them individually.</div>"}, {"time": "40000", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Programming techniques allow users to define the course of the programs since they became more interactive and graphical. The object- oriented programming (OOP) is other programming technique that lets programmers define the objects that can take definite actions based on user's data, which means it focuses on the pieces or objects you are working with.</div>"}, {"time": "66000", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">For example, a type of car that has properties as wheels, glasses and doors is the object that is included in a class of vehicles. Or a computer that has properties which are descriptive fields associated to it, as a keyboard, a monitor and a mouse; that computer is the object of a class of appliance. What did you get from this lesson? Well, you learnt the importance of programming techniques and you understood the difference between POP and OOP to retrieve or set data in the program you want to develop.</div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le02ob01re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the basic characteristics for procedural programming. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the basic characteristics for object oriented programming. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss an example of an object in an object oriented program."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What characteristics does a digital object have?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do companies dev